Lofi @VERSION@ — macOS (@ARCH@)

WHAT THIS IS
  Lofi is a Discord bot that joins a voice channel and plays lofi
  continuously. It also serves a small web dashboard for controlling it.
  This disk image contains:

    Lofi-@VERSION@.pkg   double-click installer → /usr/local/bin/lofi
    portable/lofi        the same binary, to copy anywhere you like
    LICENSE, README.md   the docs

INSTALL (recommended — the .pkg)
  1. Double-click "Lofi-@VERSION@.pkg".
     macOS will say it is from an unidentified developer: this build is not
     signed with an Apple Developer ID. Control-click the .pkg and choose
     Open if the first attempt is blocked.
  2. The installer puts the binary at /usr/local/bin/lofi.
  3. Install the two system dependencies (they are not bundled):

       brew install ffmpeg opus

  4. Check the machine, then run it:

       LOFI_TOKEN=your-bot-token lofi --check
       LOFI_TOKEN=your-bot-token lofi

INSTALL (manual — no installer)
  Drag "portable/lofi" into /usr/local/bin (or anywhere on your PATH), then:

    chmod +x /usr/local/bin/lofi
    LOFI_TOKEN=... lofi --check

FIRST RUN NOTES
  Gatekeeper: unsigned downloads are quarantined. If macOS refuses to run the
  binary, clear the quarantine attribute instead of disabling Gatekeeper:

    xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /usr/local/bin/lofi

  The dashboard is bound to 127.0.0.1:8790 by default and needs a key; the bot
  prints how to get it on startup. Read docs/SETUP.md before exposing it.

  Data (config.json, lofi.db, cache) lives in
  ~/Library/Application Support/lofi unless you set LOFI_HOME.

UNINSTALL
  The .pkg installs a single file plus docs:

    sudo rm -f /usr/local/bin/lofi
    sudo rm -rf /usr/local/share/doc/lofi
    pkgutil --forget io.github.mob5824m-wq.lofi   # forget the receipt

  Your data directory is left in place on purpose.

CPU
  @ARCH@ build. Intel Macs use the amd64 image, Apple Silicon the arm64 one.
  Pick the one matching `uname -m`.
